+// GIN transparent recovery S1 (research build): a wait that holds across a recovery.
+// The ticket is a LOGICAL WQE index (lbase + physical index when it was taken), which a recovery
+// does not change: the host publishes lbase(new) = lbase(old) + U, where [0, U) of the ending epoch
+// were executed by the responder and [U, S) are re-posted at physical [0, S - U). Inside the counted
+// region a waiter maps it: below lbase = done; else physical = logical - lbase. On an error CQE the
+// waiter publishes the Q4 record (once per epoch, without the sticky error), leaves the region and
+// parks until a new stable epoch, or a decline. Holding is bounded by the gate's waitMs (commit point
+// with the host, tsGiveUp); a declined QP or a won give-up returns ncclRemoteError and raises the
+// sticky error, as Q4 did.
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+NCCL_DEVICE_INLINE static ncclResult_t tsFail(ncclGinCtx ctx, struct ncclGinGdakiQ4* q4) {
+  if (q4 != nullptr) {
